From: Brady <brady@aioscilloscope.com>
Subject: drm/rockchip: logo: a route U-Boot gave no pixel clock is not probed (6.12)
Copyright (C) 2026 Olympian LED, Inc.

At boot the Rockchip DRM driver tries to keep the picture the boot loader
left on each output, and first reads the attached display's capabilities
(for HDMI, its EDID). When the boot loader passed no pixel clock, no display
mode can ever match, so that read only cost time: up to a second with some
HDMI sinks. The driver now skips it and closes the route as before.

---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_logo.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_logo.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_logo.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_logo.c
@@ -819,6 +819,18 @@
 
 	crtc->state->state = state;
 
+	/*
+	 * A route whose U-Boot left no pixel clock (no video,clock: a U-Boot that writes the
+	 * timings only) can match no mode below, as every mode has a
+	 * clock. Skip the connector probe, which for HDMI is an EDID read (a second with some
+	 * sinks), and let the caller close the route as for any other mismatch.
+	 */
+	if (!set->clock) {
+		dev_info(drm_dev->dev, "connector[%s]: no pixel clock from U-Boot; not probed\n",
+			 connector->name);
+		return -EINVAL;
+	}
+
 	conn_state = drm_atomic_get_connector_state(state, connector);
 	if (IS_ERR(conn_state))
 		return PTR_ERR(conn_state);
